              <lod column='[federated.05kgc8d14xgoz21903tdd0gtat7i].[sum:Number of Records:qk]' />
            </encodings>
            <customized-tooltip>
              <formatted-text>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12' underline='true'>How to read the Metrics in this table</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>There are 2 major Metrics here:</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>- # Fail Orders (Item Unavailable) by Vendor</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>- # Next Fail Order (Item Unavailable) with the same product</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Out of the first fail order with reason &quot;item Unavailable&quot; by the Vendor, the next order with the same product  can fail into different time bucket here: </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Within 1 min</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>1-15 mins</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>15-30 mins</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>30-60 mins</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Over 1 hour in the same day</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>Next day and After the next day</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>The calculation of those bucket in %  are those orders falling in the time bucket, out of the total `# Next Fail Order (Item Unavailable) with the same product `. For example, the calculation of `Next day ` would be </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>the number of orders failed with the same product happening in the next day</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>  divided by </run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>the total number of orders failed with the same product</run>
                <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'>,</run>
                <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='12'> regardless when did they fail.</run>
                <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              </formatted-text>
            </customized-tooltip>
            <style>
              <style-rule element='mark'>
                <format attr='shape' value='Icons/information_icon.png' />
              </style-rule>
            </style>
          </pane>
        </panes>
        <rows />
        <cols />
      </table>
